The '''Moon Mineralogy Mapper''' (M<sup>3</sup>) is one of two instruments of [[NASA]] that was carried by [[India]]'s first mission to the Moon, [[Chandrayaan-1]], launched October 22, 2008. It is an [[imaging spectrometer]], and the team is led by Principal investigator Carle Pieters of [[Brown University]], and managed by NASA's [[Jet Propulsion Laboratory]] (JPL).

